Below is a quick summary of what’s happening, where the “bug” lives, and how we’re fixing it:

1. Bug scenario & root cause  
   – The NumberInput component in React currently hard-codes “up/down” carets (`CaretUpGlyph`/`CaretDownGlyph`) as its spinner controls.  
   – The issue requested “other control options” (specifically, “+” and “–” buttons rather than carets).  
   – Because the component always imports and renders those two carets, there’s no way to swap in a plus/minus motif.

2. Files to patch  
   – packages/react/src/components/NumberInput/NumberInput.js  

3. What we’re going to do  
   – Replace the two icon imports at the top (`CaretUpGlyph`/`CaretDownGlyph`) with the Add16/Subtract16 icons.  
   – Replace every JSX usage of `<CaretUpGlyph …/>` with `<Add16 …/>` and `<CaretDownGlyph …/>` with `<Subtract16 …/>`.  

